==Faroese==
[[Image:Stream in gasadalur.jpg|thumb|300px|Dalsá í Gásadali]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ɔaː]|lang=fo}}<ref>{{fo-lit-FA|Vol. 2, p. 2, entry ''á<sup>1, 2</sup>''}}</ref>

===Etymology 1===
Long Old Norse /a/. often written as ''[[ā]]'' or normalized '''á''' or even ''[[aa]]'', compare Swedish, Danish, Norwegian [[å]].<ref>Vibeke Sandersen: „[http://www.dsn.dk/nfs/2002-3.htm Om bogstavet å]“ in ''Nyt fra Sprognævnet'' 2002/3 September.</ref>

====Noun====
'''á''' {{n}}

# a monophthong or dipthong, 2nd letter in the Faroese alphabet (called [ɔa])

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|á|lang=non}} (‘river’), Svabo: ''Aa'',<ref name=Sv>{{fo-lit-Sv|Aa<sup>1</sup>|1}}</ref> from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|ahwō|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{recons|akʷā-||water|lang=ine-pro}}.

====Noun====
'''á''' {{f}}

# [[brook]], [[stream]], [[river]]

=====Synonyms=====
* [[løkur]] (‘brook’)

=====Declension=====
{{fo-decl-noun-f2 (á)|á}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{sense|poetry}} '''áir''' [[renna]] [[vakur|vakrar]] [[har]] - ‘the rivers flow beautiful there’
* '''áirnar''' [[standa]] á [[svølg]]i - ‘the rivers stand on deep water’ (= it's raining a lot) (cf. [[áarføri]])
* [[um]] '''áir''' [[og]] [[gjógv|gjáir]] - ‘over rivers and gorges’ (= to travel a long way)
* fara [[yvir]] um '''á(nna)''' [[eftir]] [[vatn]]i - ‘go over the river in order to get water’ (= to look for unnecessary struggle)
* [[tað]] [[gekk]] [[sum]] [[eftir]] '''ánni''' - ‘it went like after the river’ (= it was very easy)
* [[ganga]] / [[fara]] [[í]] '''áir''' - go to the river in order to fish trouts<ref name=Sv/> (described in ''Føroysk orðabók'' 1998 as local usage in the island of [[Vágar]] about fishing trouts in a lake<ref>{{fo-lit-FO|Entry ''á<sup>2</sup>''}}</ref>)

===Etymology 3===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|á|lang=non}} (‘on, onto, in, at’). Svabo: ''aa''.<ref name="Sv2">{{fo-lit-Sv|aa<sup>2</sup>|1f.}}</ref>

====Preposition====
'''á''' (+ {{accusative}})

# [[on]], [[onto]], [[to]], [[near]], [[beside]]
# (''with fjords, bays, harbours'') to
'''á''' (+ ''dative'')
# [[on]], [[in]], [[at]]
# (''with certain place names'') in
# (''with fjords, bays, harbours'') at, in
# (''with seafaring and fishery'') at

=====Usage notes=====
''Note:'' The preposition ‘á’ is used with accusative case if the verb shows movement from one place to another, whereas it is used with dative case if the verb shows location. This is the same usage as with German ''[[auf]]'':
: '''Governing accusative'''
* [[leggja|legg]] [[bók]]ina '''á''' [[borð|borðið]] - place the book on the table
* [[hann]] [[fara|fer]] [[umborð]] '''á''' [[skip|skipið]] - he goes aboard the ship
* [[skriva]] '''á''' [[talva|talvuna]] - to write on the blackboard
* [[fara]] '''á''' [[fjall]] - to go in the mountains
: ''with fjords, bays, harbours''
* skipið [[koma|kom]] '''á''' [[Vestmanna]] - the ship came to Vestmanna
* skipið kom '''á''' [[Havn]]ina - the ship came to Tórshavn

: '''Governing dative'''
* bókin [[liggur]] '''á''' borðinum - the book is on the table
* hann er umborð '''á''' skipinum - he is aboard the ship
* [[tað]] [[standa|stendur]] '''á''' talvuni - this stands on the blackboard
* [[vera]] '''á''' fjalli - to be in the mountains (in order to roundup the sheep<ref name="Sv2"/>)
: ''place names'' (''antonym:'' [[av]])
* '''á''' [[Eiði]] - in Eiði
* '''á''' [[Glyvrar|Glyvrum]] - in Glyvrar
* '''á''' [[Húsar|Húsum]] - in Húsar
* '''á''' [[Kirkja|Kirkju]] - in Kirkja
* '''á''' [[Skáli|Skála]] - in Skáli
* '''á''' [[Velbastaður|Velbastað]] - in Velbastaður
* '''á''' [[bygd]] - in the village (countryside)
: ''with fjords, bays, harbours''
* skipið lá '''á''' Havnini - the ship lay in Tórshavn
: ''with seafaring and fishery''
* vera '''á''' [[útróður|útróðri]] - to be fishing (with a rowing boat)<ref name="Sv2"/>

===Etymology 4===
{{onomatopoeia|lang=fo}}.

====Interjection====
* '''á!'''

# [[oh]]!
# ''animal sound of the puffin ([[lundi]])''

=====Usage notes=====
* [[lundi]]n [[siga|sigur]] '''á á á''' - the puffin makes “oa oa oa”

===Etymology 5===
{{etyl|non|fo}}

====Verb====
{{head|fo|verb}}

# old 3rd person present form of {{l|fo|eiga}} (own)

